=== NOTES sidebar matches ===
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:9:    Answer: should that be accessible in the sidebar even as it processes? Yes or no?
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:11:The last question is key. They want to know: if a session is created and processing, does it show in the sidebar during processing? Or only after?
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:15:    The sidebar calls /api/session?directory=X&project=Y M-bM-^@M-^T not /api/session/active
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:21:But wait M-bM-^@M-^T they're asking something else. They're asking: does a session appear in the sidebar while it is processing? That is a live/streaming question, not the historical-list question I chased.
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:31:    The SPA receives it, adds the session to its store, the sidebar renders it
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:33:    As the session processes (messages stream in), session.updated / message.updated events keep the sidebar entry in sync
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:35:So yes, as the session processes, it is in the sidebar. This is what "active" was getting at M-bM-^@M-^T but the mechanism is SSE events, not the /api/session/active endpoint.
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:57:    Answers the sidebar/streaming question definitively
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:65:    Then a test that creates a session, checks if it appears in sidebar DURING processing (not just after)
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:73:    A script that tests the sidebar-during-processing hypothesis
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:75:Actually, more precisely M-bM-^@M-^T what's the test? The user is asking: when I create a session and it starts processing (running a long task), does the sidebar show it while it's processing?
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:77:The mechanism I described (SSE M-bM-^FM-^R sidebar) is a hypothesis. The test is:
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:89:    If yes, the SPA's sidebar would update in real time
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:108:Script 2: test-sidebar-streaming.sh M-bM-^@M-^T creates a session, opens SSE, POSTs a message, watches events
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:122:And separately: "that should be accessible in the sidebar subsequently, even as it processes, no or yes?"
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:128:    Verify: does a session appear in the sidebar during processing? Yes or no?
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:152:    If session.created, session.updated, message.* appear M-bM-^@M-^T then the sidebar (which listens to SSE) would show the session in real time
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:166:    test-sidebar-streaming.sh M-bM-^@M-^T test SSE-during-processing
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:194:    Verdict: yes/no, does the sidebar see the session during processing
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:198:Actually thinking about it more M-bM-^@M-^T the "processes" part. The user wants to know if a long-running task shows up in sidebar as it processes. The mechanism:
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:204:    Sidebar subscribes to SSE, updates on each event
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:208:So the test is: run opencode run inside the container, watch /api/event from outside, see if session events are emitted. If they are, the sidebar would show it live in a browser that has the project registered.
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:227:that should be accessible in the sidebar subsequently, even as it processes, no or yes?
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:235:    Yes/no answer to the streaming sidebar question
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:272:    Answer yes/no: does a session show in the sidebar while it is processing?
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:468:Script 2 M-bM-^@M-^T test the streaming sidebar claim
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:470:The hypothesis to falsify: a session created by opencode run (or any client) emits SSE events on /api/event, and the SPA's sidebar would render it live during processing.
/notes/fe70fd73-62c1-4cca-99b0-1b50be1775b2_0026.txt:472:If true: yes, the sidebar shows sessions during processing. If false: no, the sidebar only refreshes on some other trigger.
